 4. 🏛️ The new Washington 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Photo: J. Scott Applewhite/AP Washington's newest senators got their first taste of life on Capitol Hill this week as Democrats prepare to take control of Congress:

 Above: Sens.-elect Annie Andrews (D-S.C.), James Talarico (D-Texas) and Troy Jackson (D-Maine) walk together as they arrive for orientation. Below: Sen.-elect Abdul El-Sayed (D-Mich.) and his wife, Sarah Jukaku, ride the Senate Subway from the Capitol to the Hart Senate Office Building. Photo: Julia Demaree Nikhinson/AP 🐘 Republicans in both the House and Senate chose leaders for their next two years in the minority:

 House Minority Leader: Jim Jordan (Ohio) House Minority Whip: Tom Emmer (Minn.) House Conference Chair: Lisa McClain (Mich.) NRCC Chair (House campaign chief): Brian Jack (Ga.), replacing Richard Hudson, who lost his reelection bid . Senate Minority Leader: John Thune (S.D.) Senate Minority Whip: John Barrasso (Wyo.) Senate Conference Chair: Tom Cotton (Ark.) NRSC Chair (Senate campaign chief): Bernie Moreno (Ohio), replacing Tim Scott. More on the Senate ... House . 

 
 
