 7. 🎯 Dems put Noem on notice 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Kristi Noem attends a portrait unveiling ceremony for former Speaker Kevin McCarthy at the Capitol in September. Photo: Graeme Sloan/Bloomberg via Getty Images President Trump fired Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem in March, but Democrats aren't finished with her, Axios' Brittany Gibson writes. 

 Why it matters: Armed with commanding House and Senate majorities, they're preparing to haul the architects of Trump's mass deportation agenda before Congress to answer for their actions. Rep. Bennie Thompson of Mississippi, the top Democrat on the Homeland Security Committee, said in a letter to colleagues he'd prioritize investigating every death in DHS custody and during arrests.

 Thompson, who is running for committee chair and the subpoena power that comes with it, also plans to investigate alleged financial corruption at the agency and oversight of spending, particularly the gargantuan budget supplied by the One Big Beautiful Bill. Keep reading . 

 
 
