 8. 🎖️ 1 for the road: Good Veterans Day news 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: HUD . Map: Brad Jennings/Axios Veteran homelessness has declined by more than 50% over the past 15 years, Axios' Brad Jennings writes. 

 Numbers fell in 43 states and D.C. between 2011 and 2025, according to an Axios analysis of Department of Housing and Urban Development data. New York (-78%) , North Dakota (-77%) , Louisiana (-75%) and Georgia (-72%) saw the sharpest declines. Keep reading . Photo: Benjamin D. Applebaum/Defense Department Above: Gen. Dan Caine, chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff, walks through Corozal American Cemetery in Panama after a Veterans Day ceremony yesterday.

 
 
